1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,282
Your store can sell from more than its own pages.

2
00:00:04,282 --> 00:00:08,578
The commerce API lets your own storefront, a phone app, a point of

3
00:00:08,578 --> 00:00:13,411
sale or a back-office system sell from the same products, prices, carts and

4
00:00:13,411 --> 00:00:15,380
stock, with the same rules.

5
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:17,528
Your developers build the app.

6
00:00:17,528 --> 00:00:21,526
This video shows what you set up in the admin so it can work:

7
00:00:21,526 --> 00:00:26,180
the features, the documentation pages, sign-in, and cross-origin access.

8
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:37,160
Some stores want their own website, in any framework, that shows products and checks buyers out.

9
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:41,576
Others want a phone app, a point of sale at the counter, or

10
00:00:41,576 --> 00:00:45,130
a warehouse and accounting system connected to the store.

11
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:48,703
All of them can use the commerce API:

12
00:00:48,703 --> 00:00:54,020
the same products, prices, coupons, tax and stock holds as your storefront.

13
00:00:58,220 --> 00:01:01,112
Each commerce module has an API feature.

14
00:01:01,112 --> 00:01:03,690
You turn on the ones the app needs.

15
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:10,680
The OpenAPI feature documents the API for developers, in explorer pages they can use.

16
00:01:11,430 --> 00:01:15,949
Apps and servers sign in through your site's own sign-in server, and get

17
00:01:15,949 --> 00:01:18,150
a token to send with every call.

18
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:24,490
A storefront on another address needs your site to allow it, with a CORS policy.

19
00:01:28,676 --> 00:01:31,889
Under Tools, Features, search for API.

20
00:01:31,889 --> 00:01:35,613
Each commerce module has its own API feature:

21
00:01:35,613 --> 00:01:41,893
the Catalog API, Cart API, Checkout API, Orders API, Customers API, Shipping API

22
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:45,107
and Inventory API, plus Point of Sale.

23
00:01:45,107 --> 00:01:49,196
For a typical headless store, turn on all of them.

24
00:01:49,649 --> 00:01:51,969
Each needs its module on first.

25
00:01:51,969 --> 00:01:56,231
Here the Inventory API, which says what is in stock at each of

26
00:01:56,231 --> 00:01:58,488
your locations, is not on yet.

27
00:01:58,488 --> 00:01:59,679
Click Enable.

28
00:02:03,882 --> 00:02:09,072
To show developers the API, turn on OpenAPI on the same Features page,

29
00:02:09,072 --> 00:02:11,258
and one or more explorers.

30
00:02:11,258 --> 00:02:16,244
Swagger UI and Scalar UI let developers try calls from the browser.

31
00:02:16,244 --> 00:02:18,156
ReDoc UI is read-only.

32
00:02:18,156 --> 00:02:20,342
Click Enable on Scalar UI.

33
00:02:20,792 --> 00:02:26,090
On the OpenAPI settings page, Allow anonymous access to the API schema opens

34
00:02:26,090 --> 00:02:28,287
the description to everyone.

35
00:02:28,287 --> 00:02:34,296
By default, only a signed-in user with the View OpenAPI Content permission can read it.

36
00:02:34,296 --> 00:02:39,012
Leave it off on a live store unless you want your API to be public.

37
00:02:39,464 --> 00:02:45,366
The explorers open at slash swagger, slash scalar, and slash redoc on your site.

38
00:02:45,366 --> 00:02:48,111
The commerce API is grouped there:

39
00:02:48,111 --> 00:02:55,797
Catalog, Cart, Checkout, Inventory, Account, and for staff, Orders, Customers, Coupons, Stock, Fulfillment

40
00:02:55,797 --> 00:02:57,444
and Point of Sale.

41
00:03:01,635 --> 00:03:03,280
Guests need no sign-in:

42
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:07,363
what a shopper does before they have an account works without one.

43
00:03:07,363 --> 00:03:11,332
Everything else signs in through your site's own sign-in server.

44
00:03:11,332 --> 00:03:16,436
Turn on the OpenID features, and under Authorization Server, the token endpoint, and

45
00:03:16,436 --> 00:03:20,405
the authorization endpoint for apps that sign buyers in, are on.

46
00:03:20,856 --> 00:03:25,998
Allow authorization code flow, with Require proof key for code exchange, is for

47
00:03:25,998 --> 00:03:27,873
apps that sign people in.

48
00:03:27,873 --> 00:03:30,959
Allow client credentials flow is for servers.

49
00:03:30,959 --> 00:03:34,226
Allow refresh token flow keeps an app signed in.

50
00:03:34,226 --> 00:03:37,916
Then click Save, and the site may restart for a moment.

51
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:42,971
Then, under Token Validation, choose this tenant as the one whose tokens are accepted.

52
00:03:42,971 --> 00:03:47,110
Without this, every app that has signed in is still refused.

53
00:03:51,316 --> 00:03:55,723
An app that buyers sign in to, such as a storefront or a phone app.

54
00:03:55,723 --> 00:04:00,250
Under Applications, add one with a Client Id, a Display Name, and the

55
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:05,019
Public type, because an app in a phone or a browser cannot keep a secret.

56
00:04:05,019 --> 00:04:09,848
Tick the authorization code flow, PKCE and the refresh token flow, and add

57
00:04:09,848 --> 00:04:12,986
the redirect address your developers give you.

58
00:04:13,438 --> 00:04:15,914
Allow the profile and roles scopes.

59
00:04:15,914 --> 00:04:21,894
The roles scope tells the API the person's roles, which is where staff permissions come from.

60
00:04:21,894 --> 00:04:22,558
Save.

61
00:04:23,009 --> 00:04:26,919
A server that works on the store's behalf has no person signing in.

62
00:04:26,919 --> 00:04:30,991
First create a role for it, such as Warehouse integration, and give it

63
00:04:30,991 --> 00:04:32,919
only the permissions it needs.

64
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:38,134
Then add an application of the Confidential type, with a Client Id and

65
00:04:38,134 --> 00:04:39,952
a strong Client Secret.

66
00:04:39,952 --> 00:04:44,402
Tick the client credentials flow, and choose the role it acts as.

67
00:04:44,402 --> 00:04:48,978
Save, and give the secret only to whoever runs the server, never to

68
00:04:48,978 --> 00:04:50,670
an app or a web page.

69
00:04:54,872 --> 00:04:59,372
A storefront that runs in the browser, on another address than your site,

70
00:04:59,372 --> 00:05:01,309
needs your site to allow it.

71
00:05:01,309 --> 00:05:06,321
Turn on the CORS feature, and under Security, Cross-Origin Resource Sharing, add a

72
00:05:06,321 --> 00:05:10,821
policy for your storefront's address, such as a name, the origin, and the

73
00:05:10,821 --> 00:05:12,929
headers and methods it may use.

74
00:05:12,929 --> 00:05:15,492
Click Add Origin to add it to the list.

75
00:05:15,492 --> 00:05:20,391
The policy applies when the tenant reloads, so give your developers the policy's

76
00:05:20,391 --> 00:05:22,612
name and the address you allowed.

77
00:05:26,812 --> 00:05:32,402
A guest, not signed in, can browse products and stock, fill a cart, and check out.

78
00:05:33,152 --> 00:05:37,836
A signed-in buyer can do all of that, plus their account, orders, returns

79
00:05:37,836 --> 00:05:41,452
and shipments, and store credit and points at checkout.

80
00:05:42,202 --> 00:05:47,970
Staff, or a server, can work with orders, customers, stock, coupons and shipments,

81
00:05:47,970 --> 00:05:51,902
with the same permissions as the matching admin pages.

82
00:05:52,652 --> 00:05:59,126
The API cannot change your store's setup, such as products, prices, payment providers or taxes.

83
00:05:59,126 --> 00:06:02,396
It has no place for your own checkout fields.

84
00:06:02,396 --> 00:06:05,793
And it cannot tell other systems what happened:

85
00:06:05,793 --> 00:06:07,652
for that, use webhooks.

86
00:06:11,852 --> 00:06:13,946
A headless storefront:

87
00:06:13,946 --> 00:06:17,012
your own website, in any framework.

88
00:06:17,762 --> 00:06:22,062
A phone app buyers sign in to, to shop and follow their orders.

89
00:06:22,812 --> 00:06:25,072
A point of sale at the counter.

90
00:06:25,822 --> 00:06:27,861
A back-office integration:

91
00:06:27,861 --> 00:06:32,322
a warehouse that ships orders, or accounting that reads refunds.

92
00:06:34,322 --> 00:06:38,934
With the commerce API, your products and rules work wherever you sell.

93
00:06:38,934 --> 00:06:40,512
Thanks for watching.

